# Line endings are normalized in the repository and checked out as LF everywhere.
#
# Two reasons beyond tidiness. The bundle format is compared byte for byte between the two
# collectors, so a file that arrives with different line endings on one platform produces a
# different hash for the same content. And the translation lock records a hash per document
# to detect that the English text moved; a CRLF checkout changed every one of those hashes
# and failed the check for files nobody had touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never rewrites them.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.hve binary
